  "description": "Overview: VIBETHON is a fast-paced vibe coding hackathon by ENCIDE MACE, challenging participants to turn ideas into functional products within a short timeframe. The event encourages creative experimentation and rapid development using modern AI-powered tools and agents to accelerate ideation, design, coding, and problem-solving. With a focus on building rather than over-planning, VIBETHON creates an energetic environment where participants can explore new approaches, push their creativity, and transform simple ideas into working solutions. Guidelines: VIBETHON 2026 is an 8-hour overnight hackathon at Mar Athanasius College of Engineering, where creativity meets AI-powered innovation. Date & Time: 16th October 2026, 6 PM → 17th October 2026, 10 AM Venue: Mar Athanasius College of Engineering, Kothamangalam, Ernakulam, Kerala, India Unlike long multi-day events, VIBETHON packs the thrill into a single sprint with three structured phases: Ideation → Design → Build. Teams of 1–3 members will craft their most viable product, fueled by culture, food, and fun along the way.",
